''Note: [[Big Stan]] withdrew from the tournament on September 16. His remaining matches (Rounds 6–9) are recorded as forfeit losses, with each opponent receiving two points.''

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The block flipped.''' Taumafa 12, KAZUKI 12, Takagi 10, Jusuf 10 — four men within two points, and the head-to-heads scrambled: Taumafa beat KAZUKI, KAZUKI beat Takagi, Takagi beat Jusuf, Jusuf beat Taumafa. The Tsuda rounds will decide it on the mat, not on the tiebreakers.
* '''Ishida's resurrection.''' Written off at 3-3, the television champion's G1 is now the block's best story: the Ishida Lock has submitted Diallo, Takagi, and now KAZUKI — three submissions, and the man who ended the 1,095-day reign tapping for the first time in two years. With Tanaka (Round 8) and Taumafa (Round 9) remaining, a winning record is still live.
* '''KAZUKI's slide.''' Two straight losses for the first time since the Fall — Tosa and Anjo-Saikawa, the family giant and the written-off veteran. The Shooting Star closes with Reyes (Round 8) and Diallo (Round 9), and the block he led for five rounds may finish without him in the top two.
* '''The Tsuda collision is set.''' Taumafa vs. Takagi, Round 8, Tsuda Municipal Gymnasium — the family giant against the Dragon, the block's marquee collision, two points apart, with the block lead on the line.
* '''Reyes and Tanaka: the floor.''' Reyes 0-7, still searching; Tanaka 1-6, the betrayal a year old. The block's floor is set; the ceiling is up for grabs.

